---Properties of probe of an application gateway.
---@class azure.network.ApplicationGatewayProbePropertiesFormat
---@field protocol? azure.network.ApplicationGatewayProbePropertiesFormatProtocol|string Application Gateway protocol.
---@field host? string Host name to send the probe to.
---@field path? string Relative path of probe. Valid path starts from '/'. Probe is sent to <Protocol>://<host>:<port><path>.
---@field interval? number The probing interval in seconds. This is the time interval between two consecutive probes. Acceptable values are from 1 second to 86400 seconds.
---@field timeout? number The probe timeout in seconds. Probe marked as failed if valid response is not received with this timeout period. Acceptable values are from 1 second to 86400 seconds.
---@field unhealthyThreshold? number The probe retry count. Backend server is marked down after consecutive probe failure count reaches UnhealthyThreshold. Acceptable values are from 1 second to 20.
---@field pickHostNameFromBackendHttpSettings? boolean Whether the host header should be picked from the backend http settings. Default value is false.
---@field pickHostNameFromBackendSettings? boolean Whether the server name indication should be picked from the backend settings for Tls protocol. Default value is false.
---@field minServers? number Minimum number of servers that are always marked healthy. Default value is 0.
---@field match? azure.network.ApplicationGatewayProbeHealthResponseMatch Criterion for classifying a healthy probe response.
---@field enableProbeProxyProtocolHeader? boolean Whether to send Proxy Protocol header along with the Health Probe over TCP or TLS protocol. Default value is false.
---@field provisioningState? azure.network.ApplicationGatewayProbePropertiesFormatProvisioningState|string Provisioning states of a resource.
---@field port? number Custom port which will be used for probing the backend servers. The valid value ranges from 1 to 65535. In case not set, port from http settings will be used. This property is valid for Basic, Standard_v2 and WAF_v2 only.

