---Properties of Inbound NAT pool.
---@class azure.network.InboundNatPoolPropertiesFormat
---@field frontendIPConfiguration? azure.network.InboundNatPoolPropertiesFormatFrontendIPConfiguration Reference to another subresource.
---@field protocol azure.network.InboundNatPoolPropertiesFormatProtocol|string The transport protocol for the endpoint.
---@field frontendPortRangeStart number The first port number in the range of external ports that will be used to provide Inbound Nat to NICs associated with a load balancer. Acceptable values range between 1 and 65534.
---@field frontendPortRangeEnd number The last port number in the range of external ports that will be used to provide Inbound Nat to NICs associated with a load balancer. Acceptable values range between 1 and 65535.
---@field backendPort number The port used for internal connections on the endpoint. Acceptable values are between 1 and 65535.
---@field idleTimeoutInMinutes? number The timeout for the TCP idle connection. The value can be set between 4 and 30 minutes. The default value is 4 minutes. This element is only used when the protocol is set to TCP.
---@field enableFloatingIP? boolean Configures a virtual machine's endpoint for the floating IP capability required to configure a SQL AlwaysOn Availability Group. This setting is required when using the SQL AlwaysOn Availability Groups in SQL server. This setting can't be changed after you create the endpoint.
