---@field id? string Resource ID.
---@field name? string Name of the resource.
---@field properties? azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatInput Properties of load balancer probe.

---Load balancer probe resource.
---@class azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormat
---@field loadBalancingRules? azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatLoadBalancingRulesList The load balancer rules that use this probe.
---@field protocol azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatProtocol The protocol of the end point. If 'Tcp' is specified, a received ACK is required for the probe to be successful. If 'Http' or 'Https' is specified, a 200 OK response from the specifies URI is required for the probe to be successful.
---@field port number The port for communicating the probe. Possible values range from 1 to 65535, inclusive.
---@field intervalInSeconds? number The interval, in seconds, for how frequently to probe the endpoint for health status. Typically, the interval is slightly less than half the allocated timeout period (in seconds) which allows two full probes before taking the instance out of rotation. The default value is 15, the minimum value is 5.
---@field noHealthyBackendsBehavior? azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatNoHealthyBackendsBehavior Determines how new connections are handled by the load balancer when all backend instances are probed down.
---@field numberOfProbes? number The number of probes where if no response, will result in stopping further traffic from being delivered to the endpoint. This values allows endpoints to be taken out of rotation faster or slower than the typical times used in Azure.
---@field probeThreshold? number The number of consecutive successful or failed probes in order to allow or deny traffic from being delivered to this endpoint. After failing the number of consecutive probes equal to this value, the endpoint will be taken out of rotation and require the same number of successful consecutive probes to be placed back in rotation.
---@field requestPath? string The URI used for requesting health status from the VM. Path is required if a protocol is set to http. Otherwise, it is not allowed. There is no default value.
---@field provisioningState? azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatProvisioningState Provisioning states of a resource.

---Load balancer probe resource.
---@class azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatInput
---@field protocol azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatInputProtocol|string The protocol of the end point. If 'Tcp' is specified, a received ACK is required for the probe to be successful. If 'Http' or 'Https' is specified, a 200 OK response from the specifies URI is required for the probe to be successful.
---@field port number The port for communicating the probe. Possible values range from 1 to 65535, inclusive.
---@field intervalInSeconds? number The interval, in seconds, for how frequently to probe the endpoint for health status. Typically, the interval is slightly less than half the allocated timeout period (in seconds) which allows two full probes before taking the instance out of rotation. The default value is 15, the minimum value is 5.
---@field noHealthyBackendsBehavior? azure.network.ProbePropertiesFormatInputNoHealthyBackendsBehavior|string Determines how new connections are handled by the load balancer when all backend instances are probed down.
---@field numberOfProbes? number The number of probes where if no response, will result in stopping further traffic from being delivered to the endpoint. This values allows endpoints to be taken out of rotation faster or slower than the typical times used in Azure.
---@field probeThreshold? number The number of consecutive successful or failed probes in order to allow or deny traffic from being delivered to this endpoint. After failing the number of consecutive probes equal to this value, the endpoint will be taken out of rotation and require the same number of successful consecutive probes to be placed back in rotation.
---@field requestPath? string The URI used for requesting health status from the VM. Path is required if a protocol is set to http. Otherwise, it is not allowed. There is no default value.
